/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The proportion of payments made in cash in Switzerland is declining. It is also falling in the UK. In 2005, 70% of payments in the UK were made in cash. By 2015, this had fallen to 50% and is forecast to decline to 30% by 2025. The extent to which cash is used influences the number of banknotes printed and in circulation. Fig. 2 shows the value of banknotes in circulation in the UK over a five year period.)
/E (The proportion of payments made in cash in Switzerland is declining. It is also falling in the UK. In 2005, 70% of payments in the UK were made in cash. By 2015, this had fallen to 50% and is forecast to decline to 30% by 2025. The extent to which cash is used influences the number of banknotes printed and in circulation. Fig. 2 shows the value of banknotes in circulation in the UK over a five year period.)
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [14]
>>
